.th PTX I 12/1/77
.sh NAME
ptx \*- permuted title index
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd ptx
[
.bd \*-
]
file1 [ file2 ]
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Ptx
generates a permuted index of titles as typified by that in the
"UNIX Programmers Manual".
Non-trivial words are picked out of the titles, permuted by rotation
and sorted alphabeticaly.
.s3
Trivial words (if, but, as, etc.) are ignored.
.s3
The file \fIfile1\fR contains the titles to be permuted, one per line
and arbitrarily punctuated (max 200 characters).
.s3
Permuted titles appear on standard output.
.s3
The ``-'' flag causes
.it ptx
to produce 
.it nroff/troff
style output on \fIfile2\fR.
Lines appear as
.s3
		.xx "string one" "string two"
.s3
and by suitable macro definition, very interesting listings
can be produced.
.sh FILES
/tmp/p.tmp		temporary file
.sh DIAGNOSTICS
yes; hopefully self explanatory.
.sh BUGS
Lines appear to be limited to 100 characters with the ``-'' flag.
